@prefix pm:      <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/ontology#> .
@prefix pmc:     <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/concepts/> .
@prefix pmp:     <https://pajew.ski/prima-materia/practices/> .
@prefix rdfs:    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix skos:    <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

#
# prima-materia - two searches at the three places the first rabbinic run named
#
# The first asks what this transmission does with a success somebody has seen,
# and it found places in all three tractates. The second is the search that came
# back empty in tractate Sanhedrin on 2026-10-01, put again in a different
# tractate, where it found something; both are kept, because a negative finding
# in one corpus and a positive one in another are two findings and not a
# correction.
#

pmp:RabbinicObservedSuccessSearch a pm:Searching ;
    rdfs:label "What the transmission does with a success somebody has seen"@en, "Was die Ueberlieferung mit einem beobachteten Erfolg macht"@de ;
    pm:searchedCorpus "Babylonian Talmud, Aboda zara folios 54b to 56a, trans. Lazarus Goldschmidt, Der babylonische Talmud, vol. VII (Berlin: S. Calvary und Co., 1903), pp. 990-992; Holin folios 7a to 7b, vol. VIII (Leipzig: Otto Harrassowitz, 1909), pp. 819-822; Pesahim folios 110a to 112b, vol. II (Berlin: S. Calvary und Co., 1901), pp. 703-714" ;
    pm:searchedFor "Whether the rabbinic legal transmission, which holds the art capital and holds in several places that it has no power against a man of merit, anywhere meets a reported success of a rival practice by denying that the success occurred; and if it does not, what it does instead. The question was put because the run of 2026-10-01 read tractate Sanhedrin and found a transmission that argues at length about whether the art works and never once about a case anybody watched, and because its own notes named these three places and said that no node rested on them." ;
    pm:searchTerms "The German column of each part was separated from the Hebrew and Aramaic before reading, by keeping only lines above a measured proportion of Latin letters, because the two stand side by side and the full text interleaves them line by line. Aboda zara was located by the running head of the tractate and then by the folio head for 55a, and the whole of folios 54b to 56a was read continuously. Holin was located by the folio heads for 7a and 7b and read continuously. Pesahim was located by the folio heads for 110a to 112b and read continuously, and then searched in the German for geschieden, Geschiedene, entliess, Zauber, behex, achtgab, Paare, and in the surrounding part for the case report the lease named. The page sequence of all three parts was checked against the running heads before any page was cited." ;
    pm:searchOutcome pm:searchFoundPlace ;
    pm:searchYieldedNode pmc:AbodaZaraAfflictionsSwornToTheirHour, pmc:AbodaZaraTheIdolatersAreTalkedOver, pmc:AbodaZaraRainFollowsTheSlaughter, pmc:AbodaZaraRainOnDemandOfTheIdol, pmp:AbodaZaraSlaughterForRain, pmc:HolinTakeItYourPurposeWillNotSucceed, pmc:HolinWhiteMuleClaimNarrowedTwice, pmc:HolinThreeTimesAgainstMosesOnce, pmc:HolinTheBeastRefusesTheUntithed, pmp:HolinCommandingTheRiverToDivide, pmc:PesahimTheDangerOfPairs, pmc:PesahimWhoeverHeedsIsHeeded, pmc:PesahimTheForgottenItemOfTheList, pmc:PesahimPairsExemptions, pmc:PesahimTheDivorcedWifesSpell, pmc:PesahimTwoWomenFacingEachOther, pmc:PesahimFourActsEachWithAnExit, pmc:PesahimAmuletAgainstSixtyDemons, pmp:PesahimAmuletForSixtyDemons, pmp:PesahimSabririFormula, pmp:PesahimCounterFormulaAgainstTheSorceresses, pmc:HolinThePiousAreGreaterAfterDeath, pmc:HolinBloodFromTheStubbedToeAtones, pmc:PesahimTheCountingContestToAHundredAndOne ;
    pm:searchedBy "prima-materia, 2026-10-04" ;
    dcterms:date "2026-10-04" ;
    skos:note "The answer is that it never denies the success, in any of the three places, and that it has three different things to put in place of a denial. At Aboda zara 55a the cure is granted and the causal connection is cut, by an appointment in time that the cure was keeping anyway. On the same page the rain is granted and the connection is left standing while its sign is reversed, so that the operation works and working is the punishment. At Holin 7b and in the Pesahim material the claim itself is moved instead: narrowed after a counter-observation, discharged for whole classes of case, or qualified clause by clause until what remains is reached by several coincidences."@en ;
    skos:note "The strongest single result is not an answer to the question asked. It is the amulet at Pesahim 111b, which supplies what the search at pmp:RabbinicDefectusSearch looked for in tractate Sanhedrin and did not find: an operation with a quantity in it, a wrong value of the quantity as the named cause of failure, a sign of the failure delivered by the party operated against, and a second performance with the right value that succeeds. That search's own note said its limit was that it covered one tractate and named Sabbath 61a as the next place; the place that answers it was three tractates away in another direction."@en ;
    skos:note "What the search corrected rather than added. The note at pmc:SanhedrinNothingBesideHimEvenInSorcery reported from the secondary literature that the parallel at Holin 7b gives R. Hanina a flatter answer and that this would amount to a denial of efficacy rather than a personal exception. The flatter answer is there; the consequence is not, because the same objection and the same resolution by the man's merits follow it in this tractate too. The reading therefore refuted the conjecture that had been entered in place of the reading, which is the case AGENTS.md records at prima-materia#76 and the reason the second stage of a search is not optional."@en ;
    skos:note "What was not read, so that the next run knows where this one stopped. Of Aboda zara only folios 54b to 56a; the tractate runs to folio 76b and its opening chapters on the festivals of the nations were not opened. Of Holin only folios 7a to 7b of a tractate of a hundred and forty-two folios. Of Pesahim only folios 110a to 112b, which is the end of the tenth chapter; the account of the four cups that the pairs material hangs off begins earlier in the chapter and was not read. Of the three places the lease named, all three were read. The proven amulet at Sabbath 61a, which both this search and pmp:RabbinicDefectusSearch name as the place where a numbered condition stands, is in the first volume of this translation and was not opened in this run either."@en ;
    skos:note "A finding about the way, entered here as well as in the table of access routes because it cost this run a search that should not have to be repeated. The identifier pattern derbabylonischet<NN>gold holds for the seventh volume of this translation and for no other; derbabylonischet02gold, derbabylonischet08gold and derbabylonischet01gold have no item behind them. The whole translation is reachable as derbabylonischet01unse to derbabylonischet08unse, found by searching the archive's own catalogue for the title and the translator rather than by guessing an identifier. A second, later translation by the same man exists on the same archive as twelve items named band-1 to band-12, published between 1929 and 1936 with a different volume division; its first volume carries no full text, and its pagination is not the pagination of the volumes cited here. Citing a page from the one in the belief that it is the other is the error this note exists to prevent."@en .

pmp:RabbinicObservedSuccessDefectusSearch a pm:Searching ;
    rdfs:label "Whether the three places name a condition under which an operation would have failed"@en, "Ob die drei Stellen eine Bedingung nennen, unter der eine Verrichtung misslungen waere"@de ;
    pm:searchedCorpus "Babylonian Talmud, Aboda zara folios 54b to 56a, trans. Lazarus Goldschmidt, Der babylonische Talmud, vol. VII (Berlin: S. Calvary und Co., 1903), pp. 990-992; Holin folios 7a to 7b, vol. VIII (Leipzig: Otto Harrassowitz, 1909), pp. 819-822; Pesahim folios 110a to 112b, vol. II (Berlin: S. Calvary und Co., 1901), pp. 703-714" ;
    pm:searchedFor "The question pmp:RabbinicDefectusSearch put to tractate Sanhedrin on 2026-10-01 and answered with nothing, put again to the three places opened here: any sentence saying what would show that a prescribed operation of this transmission had not worked, what to do if it did not, a term after which nothing more comes, a repetition on failure, or a defect in the operator or the material that would prevent the effect." ;
    pm:searchTerms "The separated German of all three parts was searched for misslingt, misslang, Misslingen, wirkt nicht, vergeblich, umsonst, gelingt, gelingt nicht, nicht gelingen, unwirksam, wiederhol, Frist, Probe, pruefen, Zeichen, vermag nicht, nichts geschieht, nuetzt nichts, and for the numerals one to sixty spelt out in the Pesahim part, where numbers carry the rule. Each part was then read through continuously so that a condition standing without any of those words would be seen." ;
    pm:searchOutcome pm:searchFoundPlace ;
    pm:searchYieldedNode pmc:PesahimAmuletAgainstSixtyDemons, pmc:HolinTakeItYourPurposeWillNotSucceed ;
    pm:searchedBy "prima-materia, 2026-10-04" ;
    dcterms:date "2026-10-04" ;
    skos:note "Two finds, of very different strength, and the weaker one is the one the search was shaped to catch. The strong find is the amulet of Pesahim 111b, where a wrong number in the formula is the stated cause of the failure and the right number repairs it. The weak find is R. Hanina's words at Holin 7b, take it, your purpose will not succeed, which is a prediction that a particular operation by a particular person will fail; it is a condition of failure of somebody else's operation and not of one this transmission prescribes, and the discussion immediately makes the general claim safe by the man's merits, so nothing in the transmission turns on whether the prediction held."@en ;
    skos:note "What still did not come back, after three tractates. No term, no count of attempts, no repetition on failure, and no defect in a material. The remedies the Pesahim part prescribes are given as lists of alternatives any one of which suffices - five for the thirst at night, three for the two women in the street - and a list of sufficient alternatives is the opposite of a condition of failure: it says what else to try and never when to stop. Of the operations the two earlier files report of this transmission's own teachers, the calf, the field of cucumbers, the river and the ass, not one carries a condition of any kind."@en ;
    skos:note "The limit of this search, stated in the same terms as its predecessor's. It covers five printed pages of one tractate, four of a second and twelve of a third, out of three tractates running to several hundred folios, and it reaches no part of this transmission outside the Babylonian Talmud. The place in it where a numbered condition is known to stand, the proven amulet of tractate Sabbath, has now been named by two searches and opened by neither."@en .
